      "title": "Finishing, not native 4K generation",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Run only after approving the native clip\nRefresh ComfyUI after generating HFL, then choose its native MKV in node 1. The dropdown scans input and output storage. It does not require a re-upload.\n\n2160-pixel short edge, capped at 3840 pixels on the long edge, with the native aspect ratio preserved. For 1344 x 768 / 768 x 1344 masters, expect approximately **3780 x 2160 / 2160 x 3780**. This is 4K-class, not an exact 16:9 UHD crop. No stretch, synthetic frame-rate interpolation or source-frame insertion.\n\nThe upscaler uses nine-frame temporal batches, four-frame overlap, uniform last-batch padding, LAB color correction and zero additional input/latent noise. Keep the native master: generative upscaling can alter fine facial features even with noise controls at zero.\n\nCompare native and finished faces at the beginning, middle and end, and through motion. Reject the finish if identity is worse. Increase batch size to 13 or 17 only after a successful GPU test with enough headroom.\n\nNative MKV masters are FFV1 RGB16 with the generated audio retained; they may not play in a browser. The MP4 is the browser preview.\n\nPlanning target: H200-class 141 GB VRAM, 256 GB system RAM and 300 GB volume. Not a measured hardware minimum. No GPU inference has been certified."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Run only after approving the native clip\nRefresh ComfyUI after generating HFL, then choose its native MKV in node 1. The dropdown scans input and output storage. It does not require a re-upload.\n\n2160-pixel short edge, capped at 3840 pixels on the long edge, with the native aspect ratio preserved. For 1344 x 768 / 768 x 1344 masters, expect approximately **3780 x 2160 / 2160 x 3780**. This is 4K-class, not an exact 16:9 UHD crop. No stretch, synthetic frame-rate interpolation or source-frame insertion.\n\nThe upscaler uses nine-frame temporal batches, four-frame overlap, uniform last-batch padding, LAB color correction and zero additional input/latent noise. Keep the native master: generative upscaling can alter fine facial features even with noise controls at zero.\n\nCompare native and finished faces at the beginning, middle and end, and through motion. Reject the finish if identity is worse. Increase batch size to 13 or 17 only after a successful GPU test with enough headroom.\n\nNative MKV masters are FFV1 RGB16 with the generated audio retained; they may not play in a browser. The MP4 is the browser preview.\n\nPlanning target: H200-class 141 GB VRAM, 256 GB system RAM and 300 GB volume. Not a measured hardware minimum. No GPU inference has been certified."
      }
    }
